  "title": "# Leftovers: finish every nearly-done build (Brett, Oct 31 night) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/ru…",
  "asked": "# Leftovers: finish every nearly-done build (Brett, Oct 31 night) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md and _claude/persona.md first. Opus, one session, no sub-agents. Git login on this server works now: plain `git push` works. The builds store (Urgent master cleanup) is the source of truth; orchestrator.json files are read-only exports. Read each build's steps from the store, do the pending steps, tick them in the store. Finish these, in this order, one at a time (commit after each): 1. urgent / urgent-builds: s12 (last step). 2. refactor / orch-pending-sync: s3. 3. refactor / veto-everywhere: s3 and s9. If a step lives in MossesX/axHub, clone it next to this worktree, do it there, test (pnpm test on Node 22 via docker node:22 if needed) and push its main too. 4. refactor / agent-voice: s9 (status 'waiting': find what it waits on; if it waits on Brett, put a banner item and skip). 5. angel / live-key-checks: s7 and s12. 6. angel / ui-review: s9. 7. angel / audio-extract: s7. 8. angel / audio-output-recorder: shows running 0/5 but the recorder and its axHub control are on main (e46b8079, 08f84bf3). Check each step against main; tick what is really done, do what is not. 9. Bug: in apps/axhub-web's approvals log, entries for tools that ran without approval (vps.build_start, build_land, build_stop, build_list) have a 'The request' button that opens an empty request page. Show those entries' details inline (tool, arguments, who ran it, time, result) or hide the button for them. Test it. Do NOT start home-cards (0/18), plugin-floatable or any other pending-but-unstarted build. Do not touch archived builds. Rules: framework controls + theme/scale tokens only, nothing handwritten that doesn't conform to hot-swappable assets. Run the full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks (failures that also fail on clean main from this machine's Node 20 / sync-held files are fine; say so). Screenshots for UI changes go to UI Review through the ui-review-item@1 schema with a group named 'Leftovers - <date time>'. After each finished build: git fetch, merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main`. Never force-push main. End with a plain-English report at _claude/builds/reports/leftovers.md: for every item, what it was, what was wrong or missing, what changed, tests, commit. Anything you couldn't do goes in the console banner with the reason. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
